.TH "ipsvd\-cdb" "8" 
.SH NAME
ipsvd\-cdb \- create constant database from ipsvd instructions directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]ipsvd\-cdb\f[R] \f[I]cdb\f[R] \f[I]cdb.tmp\f[R] \f[I]dir\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]ipsvd\-cdb\f[R] scans the directory \f[I]dir\f[R], and compiles all
relevant information for an internet protocol service daemon,
\f[B]ipsvd\f[R](7), into the newly created constant database
\f[I]cdb.tmp\f[R].
If \f[I]cdb.tmp\f[R] exists, it will be destroyed.
\f[B]ipsvd\-cdb\f[R] then renames \f[I]cdb.tmp\f[R] to \f[I]cdb\f[R].
If \f[I]cdb\f[R] exists, it will be destroyed.
.PP
\f[B]ipsvd\-cdb\f[R] skips filenames starting with two dots.
.PP
If \f[B]ipsvd\-cdb\f[R] has trouble building the constant database, it
exits with an error message, and leaves \f[I]cdb\f[R] unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
ipsvd(7), tcpsvd(8), udpsvd(8), ipsvd\-instruct(5)
.PP
https://smarden.org/ipsvd/
